    "result_text": "All 265 tests pass, BUILD SUCCESS. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires owner responses to include a `displayName` field formatted as `'LastName, FirstName'`. Since both the create response (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and read response (`RespondWithOwner`) map the `Owner` entity through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, deriving the field in the mapper covers the response consistently.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct expression mapping on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nThe new `Cp06Tests.coreDisplayName` passes (creates an owner with `firstName=\"John\"`, expects `$.displayName` = `\"LastName, John\"`), and the full suite (265 tests) is green.",
